From: mwlaboratories <info@mwlabs.be>
Subject: [PATCH] media: venus: venc: size input buffers to the firmware requirement

venc_queue_setup() asks the firmware for its input buffer requirements
(HFI_PROPERTY_CONFIG_BUFFER_REQUIREMENTS) but keeps only the count. The
size handed to vb2, and to the firmware as alloc_len, comes from the
driver's own NV12 formula. On HFI v4 (sdm845) there is no driver-side
buffer calculation, so the firmware's number is the authority.

Since "drop extra padding in NV12 raw size calculation" (7.4) that
formula is 12 KiB smaller than before, and smaller than the downstream
VENUS_BUFFER_SIZE layout the sdm845 firmware was written against. On the
OnePlus 6 the encoder then produced no frame in 60 s.

Take the larger of the two sizes, and log both under dynamic debug so
the gap can be measured.

Status: hypothesis until tested on the OnePlus 6 (sdm845, venus 5.2).
---
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/venc.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/venc.c
@@ -1064,7 +1064,8 @@
 	return ret;
 }
 
-static int venc_out_num_buffers(struct venus_inst *inst, unsigned int *num)
+static int venc_out_num_buffers(struct venus_inst *inst, unsigned int *num,
+				unsigned int *size)
 {
 	struct hfi_buffer_requirements bufreq;
 	int ret;
@@ -1074,6 +1075,7 @@
 		return ret;
 
 	*num = bufreq.count_actual;
+	*size = bufreq.size;
 
 	return 0;
 }
@@ -1084,7 +1086,7 @@
 {
 	struct venus_inst *inst = vb2_get_drv_priv(q);
 	struct venus_core *core = inst->core;
-	unsigned int num, min = 4;
+	unsigned int num, fw_size = 0, min = 4;
 	int ret;
 
 	if (*num_planes) {
@@ -1136,7 +1138,7 @@
 	case V4L2_BUF_TYPE_VIDEO_OUTPUT_MPLANE:
 		*num_planes = inst->fmt_out->num_planes;
 
-		ret = venc_out_num_buffers(inst, &num);
+		ret = venc_out_num_buffers(inst, &num, &fw_size);
 		if (ret)
 			break;
 
@@ -1147,6 +1149,15 @@
 		sizes[0] = venus_helper_get_framesz(inst->fmt_out->pixfmt,
 						    inst->out_width,
 						    inst->out_height);
+		/*
+		 * The firmware reports the input buffer size it needs (HFI v4
+		 * has no driver-side calculation). Never hand it less.
+		 */
+		dev_dbg(core->dev,
+			"venc: input %ux%u, driver size %u, firmware size %u, count %u\n",
+			inst->out_width, inst->out_height, sizes[0], fw_size,
+			*num_buffers);
+		sizes[0] = max(sizes[0], fw_size);
 		inst->input_buf_size = sizes[0];
 		break;
 	case V4L2_BUF_TYPE_VIDEO_CAPTURE_MPLANE:
